eturn To Homepage With a mission to serve as a ‘Center of Excellence’, Koç University aims to contribute to science at a global level by bringing together exceptionally talented youth with distinguished faculty members.Koç University is dedicated to excellence in both research and teaching and is ranked 1st in Türkiye in many national and international rankings, such as Times Higher Education World University Ranking (global rank: 301-350), URAP Türkiye Ranking, YÖK Research Universities’ Ranking, and Times Higher Education Interdisciplinary Science Ranking (global rank 28) . Koç University fosters an outstanding interdisciplinary research environment for the faculty members and houses state-of-the-art central facilities and multidisciplinary research centers. Koç University's Human Resources Strategy for Researchers As of October 2020, the Koç University Working Group for the development and implementation of a “Human Resources Strategy for Researchers“ has submitted a revised application for the European Commission’s “HR Excellence in Research Award“. This webpage is dedicated to the official strategy documents of and the future developments regarding this process. The Working Group will be updating this portal with developments as the university remedies its gaps and implements its strategy. × Filter by Departments Administrative Sciences and Economics Archaeology and History of Art Chemical and Biological Engineering Chemistry College of Engineering – Optical Microsystems Laboratory Computer Engineering Electrical and Electronics Engineering Industrial Engineering Law School Mathematics Mechanical Engineering Media and Visual Arts Physics Psychology School of Medicine School of Nursing Sociology Filter by Positions Full Professor Full-time Faculty Instructor Laboratory Instructor Postdoctoral Researcher Tenure Track Faculty Tenure Track Faculty Position in the School of Medicine The Department of Biophysics at the Koç University School of Medicine invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor position. Tenure Track Faculty Position in the School of Nursing Koç University School of Nursing, located in the Health Sciences Campus at Topkapı, aims to achieve excellence in education, research, and practice by bringing together the best students, faculty, and researchers with a value-added approach, and invites academics in Women’s Health Nursing (2 faculty members), Public Health Nursing (1 faculty member) and Nursing Management (2 faculty members) to apply for full-time faculty positions. Instructor Position in English Language Center Koç University is one of the premier research institutions in Turkey. Its English Language Center   \n(ELC) provides intensive language instruction to prepare students for the university’s English\u0002\nmedium academic programs. It plays a pivotal role in the students’ transition to university life with   \napproximately 900 students enrolled each year and 50 faculty members. Faculty Position in Electrical and Electronics Engineering Koç University College of Engineering invites exceptional candidates to apply for full-time faculty positions in Electrical and Electronics Engineering. Outstanding applicants with strong theoretical and experimental research contributions in all areas of electrical and electronics engineering are invited to apply. Postdoctoral Researcher Position in Wearable Biosensors Koç University – College of Engineering \t\t\t\t\n\t\tThe Optical Microsystems Laboratory (OML ) under direction of Prof. Hakan Urey at Koç University, Istanbul – Türkiye invites applications for a Postdocto Tenure-Track  Faculty Positions in the Chemistry Department Koç University, a foundation-supported, non-profit institution of higher education in Istanbul, Türkiye, invites applications for tenure-track junior faculty positions in all areas of chemistry. Prior Tenure Track Faculty Position in Mechanical Engineering Koç University College of Engineering invites applications for full-time faculty positions in Mechanical Engineering starting in Fall 2026. Strong applicants in all areas of mechanical engineering, preferably with interdisciplinary research interests, and at all academic levels with an exemplary record of research and publication record will be considered. Tenure Track Faculty Position in Industrial Engineering The Department of Industrial Engineering at Koç University invites applications and nominations for full-time faculty positions to start in Fall 2026. We seek outstanding candidates in all areas of industrial engineering, preferably with a strong background in operations research. The candidates are expected to complement and enhance the current research and education portfolio of the department and preferably have interests in one or more of the following application areas: data analytics, energy systems, financial engineering, healthcare, production and service systems, supply chain and logistics, and sustainable operations. Individuals at all ranks are encouraged to apply (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor). Tenure Track Faculty Position in Electrical and Electronics Engineering Koç University College of Engineering invites exceptional candidates to apply for full-time faculty positions in Electrical and Electronics Engineering. Outstanding applicants with strong theoretical and experimental research contributions in all areas of electrical and electronics engineering are invited to apply. Applicants should have a bold,  interdisciplinary research agenda capable of making substantial and transformative impacts across multiple disciplines. Tenure Track Faculty Position in Computer Engineering Koç University College of Engineering invites applications for full-time faculty positions in Computer Science and Engineering starting in Fall 2025 or Spring 2026. We seek outstanding candidates with significant contributions in all computer science and engineering research areas. The ideal candidate will have a visionary research agenda, an exceptional research and publication track record, and a strong commitment to academic excellence and innovation. The successful candidate will demonstrate dedication to undergraduate and graduate education and foster an inclusive learning environment. Tenure Track Faculty Position  in Chemical and Biological Engineering The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering at Koç University in Istanbul, Türkiye, is actively seeking a highly motivated individual for a full-time faculty position at all levels. The candidate should have a Ph.D. in Chemical and/or Biological Engineering, Biotechnology, or a closely related field. We are looking for outstanding individuals who can build strong research and teaching programs and develop into intellectual leaders. Candidates at all academic ranks with an exemplary research and publication record will be considered. Tenure Track Faculty Position in the Law School Koç University invites applications for full-time faculty positions in the Law School. Koç University is a private, non-profit institution of higher education, founded in 1993. It has been ranked as the best university in Türkiye, 52nd in Young University Rankings and has been placed among the top 400 universities in the World University Rankings, by the Times Higher Education in 2024. Instructor Position in Marketing The College of Administrative Sciences and Economics at Koç University invites applications for a teaching-focused Instructor position in Marketing, starting September 2026. The successful candidate may teach undergraduate and graduate marketing courses. Responsibilities include curriculum development, assessment management, and student advising. Koç University offers a competitive salary and benefits package. Full-time instructor position in Media and Communications Koç University's Department of Media and Visual Arts (MAVA) invites applications for a full-time instructor position to start in September 2026. Applications submitted by January 19, 2026 will receive full consideration, with later applications reviewed as needed until the position is filled. Tenure-Track  Faculty Positions in Media and Communications Koç University’s Department of Media and Visual Arts (MAVA) invites applications for a full-time open-rank faculty position to start in September 2026. Applications submitted by January 19, 2026 will receive full consideration, with later applications reviewed as needed until the position is filled. Full-Time Faculty Members of any rank in Sociology The Department of Sociology at Koç University invites applications for a full-time faculty position of any rank to begin September 2026. The successful candidate will have an active research agenda and a demonstrable record of original research in the field. The candidate is expected to engage in the intellectual life of our department with diverse theoretical and methodological interests, and to teach broadly on the Department’s curriculum as appropriate. Full-Time Faculty Members of any rank in Clinical Psychology Koç University Department of Psychology has vacancies for full-time faculty positions specializing in Clinical Psychology to commence in Fall 2026. We will consider promising early-career applicants as well as mid-career or senior applicants with an established research agenda. Clinical psychology faculty candidates are expected to have research programs and to teach undergraduate and graduate level courses in clinical psychology in English, supervise clinical practicum in Turkish, and advise MA theses and PhD dissertations. Tenure-Track Faculty Positions in Physics Department Koç University, a foundation-supported, non-profit institution of higher education in Istanbul, Türkiye, invites applications for a tenure-track full-time faculty position in Experimental or Theoretical Physics that will complement and/or expand the current research activities of the Physics Department. Current research areas include mathematical physics, biological physics, cold atoms, condensed and soft matter physics, gravitation, spectroscopy, micro/nano photonic materials and devices, quantum technologies, quantum optics, solid-state lasers, ultrafast optics, and biomedical optics. Full Professor of Archaeology and History of Art at Koç University acting as the Director of the Koç University Center for Byzantine Studies (GABAM) Koç University invites applications at the level of Full Professor for the position of Director of the Koç University Center for Byzantine Studies (GABAM) and a fulltime faculty position at the Department of Archaeology and History of Art (ARHA).  The anticipated start date of the position is Fall 2025. Candidates should have an academic background in Late Antique and/or Byzantine archaeology, history of art, and/or cultural heritage management and a demonstrable, internationally recognized outstanding research and teaching track record related to Late Antique and Byzantine Studies. A Laboratory Instructor Position for Chemistry Department Koç University Chemistry Department invites applications for the Laboratory Instructor position starting in Fall 2025. The Laboratory Instructor establishes a positive learning environment for undergraduate students, ensures the laboratory’s smooth operation, and teaches undergraduate laboratories within the scope and guidelines established by the department. Instructor Position for Mathematics Department The Department of Mathematics at Koç University, a leading foundation supported, non-profit institution of higher education in Istanbul, Türkiye, invites applications for a full-time (12-month) lecturer position preferably starting in September 2025. Tenure-Track  Faculty Positions in the Department of Chemistry and KUHyTech Center The Department of Chemistry, in collaboration with Koç University Hydrogen Technologies Center (KUHyTech), in Istanbul, Türkiye, invites applications for a full-time faculty position. Türkiye, invites applications for a full-time faculty position. No positions found matching your search criteria. 1 2 3 4 Helpful Links Recruitment Policy Koç University is committed to open, transparent and merit-based recruitment policies through fair processes and highly values a diverse working environment, with the focus on continuous development, diversity, interdisciplinary research, collaborative environment, well-being, mobility and equality in the workplace. More Wellbeing and satisfaction are surveyed annually and there are annual performance and development reviews, to ensure the right balance between the goals of the unit (Section/Department, etc) and the skills development of individual staff and the way they work. We believe that our ethical values are crucial for maintaining a success-focused and peaceful working environment in the University. “Rules of Ethical Behavior and Implementation Principles” has been prepared to ensure that these values are equally widespread among all academic and administrative staff and transmitted to future generations. In 2020 Koç University was granted with HR Excellence in Research Award. As a holder of the HR Excellence in Research Award, the University is committed to participating in both national and European evaluation and benchmarking exercises to ensure that faculty, students, researchers and administrative are recruited through a transparent application, evaluation and selection cycle. HR Strategy for Researchers Equal Opportunity Koç University is committed to ensuring equal employment opportunity to all qualified individuals and foster a diverse community.  The University believes a diverse workforce will enhance its ability to fulfill the mission of research, education and public service. More Koç University encourages proactive initiatives to increase diversity and provide equal opportunity to all applicants and employees.  A competitive recruitment process includes the sourcing, screening, and selection of employees and promotes equal opportunity by informing potential applicants of job vacancies within the University. Learning and Development Human Resources Department provides learning and development opportunities for all administrative staff to support their behavioral and professional growth in line with their corporate, functional, and individual requirements. Detailed Information HR in Research Excellence HRS4R is a voluntary process where universities, research institutions and organizations can contribute to the development of an attractive European labor market for researchers. Detailed Information Rumelifeneri Yolu 34450 Sarıyer, İstanbul / TR information@ku.edu.tr Tel: +90 212 338 1000 MENU Research Academics Explore Contact Admission QUICK MENU Prospective Student KU Student Faculty Member KU Alumni Administrative Staff Visitor Information on Personal Data Privacy Download KUHub Mobile! English Cookie Policy Cookies are used to personalize content and ads, to provide social media features and to analyze our traffic. You can accept all cookies by selecting \"Allow All\" or you can edit the settings by selecting \"Customize my cookie settings\". When you visit a website, information is stored in your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information may be about you, your preferences or your device, and is often used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually identify you directly, it is meant to provide you with a more personalized web experience. You can choose not to allow some cookies. Click on the different category headings to learn more and change our default settings. Click here to view our cookie policy. Allow All Reject All Customize My Cookie Settings Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be turned off in our systems. Statistical Cookies These cookies are used to provide insight into how we can improve our service to all our users and to understand how you interact with our website as an anonymous user.