es Home Postdoctoral Researcher Position in Wearable Biosensors Home Postdoctoral Researcher Position in Wearable Biosensors Back to Job Search Postdoctoral Researcher Position in Wearable Biosensors Koç University – College of Engineering The Optical Microsystems Laboratory (OML ) under direction of Prof. Hakan Urey at Koç University, Istanbul – Türkiye invites applications for a Postdoctoral Researcher position in a translational research project focused on the development of novel wearable microfabricated biosensors . The successful candidate will contribute to the design, fabrication, and validation of next-generation wearable biosensing platforms aimed at real-time biomarker monitoring and precision health applications. The project integrates bioengineering, molecular biology, materials science, and translational biomedical research. Research Scope and Methodology Our research program focuses on: Wearable biosensor system design, fabrication and integration Surface functionalization and biomolecular immobilization strategies Ex vivo and In vivo validation using relevant biological samples Translational development from prototype to preclinical evaluation Required Qualifications PhD degree in Engineering, Molecular Biology, Biomedical Engineering, Materials Science, Biophysics, or a related discipline Demonstrated experience in biosensor development and characterization Strong experimental hands-on experience in at least one of the following areas: Photolithography, MEMS, or flexible microfabrication techniques Microfluidic device design for biofluid sampling (e.g., sweat, interstitial fluid) Biosensing and continuous metabolite monitoring Microneedle-based sampling systems Wireless/passive sensor integration approaches Motivation to conduct translational research bridging laboratory innovation and real-world biomedical applications Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary environment Application Process Applicants should submit: A cover letter describing research interests and motivation Curriculum vitae Contact information for at least two referees Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Fellowships and Career Development: Koç University actively supports advancing careers of postdoctoral researchers and their applications for competitive national and international programs, including: TÜBİTAK 2236 Co-Circulation Scheme TÜBİTAK 2218 National Postdoctoral Research Fellowship EMBO Postdoctoral Fellowships Marie Skłodowska-Curie Postdoctoral Fellowships Koç University institutional postdoctoral fellowship schemes ERC-Starting grant applications Koç University is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to excellence in research and education. Candidates should send e-mail with Subject line: Wearable Sensors Postdoctoral Position Addressed to Prof. Hakan Urey, Email: hurey@ku.edu.tr Rumelifeneri Yolu 34450 Sarıyer, İstanbul / TR information@ku.edu.tr Tel: +90 212 338 1000 MENU Research Academics Explore Contact Admission QUICK MENU Prospective Student KU Student Faculty Member KU Alumni Administrative Staff Visitor Information on Personal Data Privacy Download KUHub Mobile! English Cookie Policy Cookies are used to personalize content and ads, to provide social media features and to analyze our traffic. You can accept all cookies by selecting \"Allow All\" or you can edit the settings by selecting \"Customize my cookie settings\". When you visit a website, information is stored in your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information may be about you, your preferences or your device, and is often used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually identify you directly, it is meant to provide you with a more personalized web experience. You can choose not to allow some cookies. Click on the different category headings to learn more and change our default settings. Click here to view our cookie policy. Allow 