Pages Home Tenure-Track  Faculty Positions in the Chemistry Department Home Tenure-Track  Faculty Positions in the Chemistry Department Back to Job Search Tenure-Track  Faculty Positions in the Chemistry Department Koç University, a foundation-supported, non-profit institution of higher education in Istanbul, Türkiye, invites applications for tenure-track junior faculty positions in all areas of chemistry. Priority will be given to candidates specializing in polymer and/or organic chemistry whose research will enhance and broaden the Department’s existing strengths. Applicants should have an outstanding publication record, a compelling vision for future research, and postdoctoral or industrial R&D experience. Appointments are expected to begin in October 2026. The Department of Chemistry at Koç University is a dynamic and internationally recognized community, with faculty members recruited from leading institutions worldwide and top-tier, highly motivated undergraduate and graduate students. The department offers a supportive, collaborative, and intellectually stimulating environment. Koç University is dedicated to excellence in both research and teaching and is ranked 1st in Türkiye and 52nd globally in the Times Higher Education (THE) Young University Rankings 2024. Koç University fosters an outstanding interdisciplinary research environment for the faculty members and houses state-of-the-art central facilities and multidisciplinary research centers. Koç University, as a leading Research University in Türkiye and a center of excellence, is hosting 28 out of 48 European Research Council (ERC) Grant recipients in Türkiye and the largest recipient of Horizon 2020 research funding in the nation. Upcoming faculty members are eligible to apply for European Union Marie-Curie Actions and Turkish Science Foundation TUBITAK 2232 International Fellowship for Outstanding Researchers Program. Successful candidates will be expected to build and sustain a globally competitive, externally funded research program, teach undergraduate and graduate-level courses, supervise graduate and undergraduate student research and contribute to departmental and university service. The medium of instruction is English. Salary will be competitive and commensurate with experience. Side benefits include housing aid, health insurance and financial support for K12 education of candidates’ children. Applications should be submitted online at academicjobsonline.org and should consist of the following materials: (a) cover letter (including a summary of past and ongoing research) (b) curriculum vitae and publication list, (c) research plan, (d) teaching statement, and (e) three letters of recommendation. Applications will be considered until the position is filled. Rumelifeneri Yolu 34450 Sarıyer, İstanbul / TR information@ku.edu.tr Tel: +90 212 338 1000 MENU Research Academics Explore Contact Admission QUICK MENU Prospective Student KU Student Faculty Member KU Alumni Administrative Staff Visitor Information on Personal Data Privacy Download KUHub Mobile! English Cookie Policy Cookies are used to personalize content and ads, to provide social media features and to analyze our traffic. You can accept all cookies by selecting \"Allow All\" or you can edit the settings by selecting \"Customize my cookie settings\". When you visit a website, information is stored in your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information may be about you, your preferences or your device, and is often used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually identify you directly, it is meant to provide you with a more personalized web experience. You can choose not to allow some cookies. Click on the different category headings to learn more and change our default settings. Click here to view our cookie policy. Allow All Reject All Customize My Cookie Settings Necessary Cookies These cookies are necessary for the website to function and cannot be turned o